hwui's critical natives as ART calls them (ADR-0043 test 2).

The host flavor's files take the host side of every test of __ANDROID__ (tools/soong_plan.py's make_tree), which
gives graphics_jni_helpers.h's CRITICAL_JNI_PARAMS layoutlib's JNIEnv* and jclass: a host JVM does not know
@CriticalNative and passes them to every native. The guest's VM is ART, which calls the natives that
framework.jar's graphics classes mark @CriticalNative without them, as on Android. With the host side, such a
native reads its arguments two registers late (Font.nGetPackedStyle loaded through a null pointer at the first
Typeface). So the macros take the Android side, whatever the host side does.

--- a/frameworks/base/libs/hwui/jni/graphics_jni_helpers.h
+++ b/frameworks/base/libs/hwui/jni/graphics_jni_helpers.h
@@ -27,13 +27,8 @@
 // and they need all the JNI methods to have JNIEnv* and jclass/jobject as their first two arguments.
 // The following macro allows to have those arguments when compiling for host while omitting them when
 // compiling for Android.
-#ifdef __ANDROID__
 #define CRITICAL_JNI_PARAMS
 #define CRITICAL_JNI_PARAMS_COMMA
-#else
-#define CRITICAL_JNI_PARAMS JNIEnv*, jclass
-#define CRITICAL_JNI_PARAMS_COMMA JNIEnv*, jclass,
-#endif
 
 namespace android {
 
